      "text": "First, we need to calculate the slant height of the pyramid, which will help us find the area of the four triangular faces. This can be done using the Pythagorean theorem, as shown below:\n\n[\ntext{{slant_height_sq}} = text{{base_half}}^2 + text{{height_sq}}\n]\n\nNext, we can calculate the area of the four triangular faces, each with base 10 cm and height equal to the slant height calculated in the first step.\n\n[\ntext{{total_triangular_face_area_sq}} = left( 2 times 10 times text{{slant_height}} right)\n]\n\nNow, we can calculate the area of the square base.\n\n[\ntext{{square_base_area_sq}} = 10^2\n]\n\nFinally, we can add the area of each triangular face and the area of the square base to find the total surface area of the pyramid. This can be done as follows:\n\n[\ntext{{total_surface_area_sq}} = text{{total_triangular_face_area_sq}} + text{{square_base_area_sq}}\n]\n\nLet's put all these steps together in the code.\n```less\nimport math\n\ndef calculate_surface_area(base_side_length, peak_height):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function calculates the total surface area of a right pyramid with a square base.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    base_side_length (float): The length of the side of the square base of the pyramid.\n    peak_height (float): The height from the center of the base to the peak of the pyramid.\n    \n    Returns:\n    float: The total surface area of the pyramid.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Calculate the slant height of the pyramid using the Pythagorean theorem\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(base_side_length**2 + peak_height**2)\n    \n    # Calculate the area of the four triangular faces\n    total_triangular_face_area = 4 * (1/2) * base_side_length * slant_height\n    \n    # Calculate the area of the square base\n    square_base_area = base_side_length**2\n    \n    # Calculate the total surface area\n    total_surface_area = total_triangular_face_area + square_base_area\n    \n    return total_surface_area\n```",
