      "text": "To find the surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces. \n\nFirst, we calculate the area of the base:\nThe base is a square with side length 10 cm, so the area is 10 * 10 = 100 square centimeters.\n\nNext, we calculate the slant height of the pyramid. The slant height is the height of one of the triangular faces. To find it, we use the Pythagorean theorem:\nThe height of the pyramid is 12 cm, and the base of the pyramid (half of the square base) is 5 cm.\nTo find the slant height, we have a right triangle with legs of 5 cm and 12 cm, so the slant height is √(5^2 + 12^2) = 13 cm.\n\nNow, we can calculate the area of each triangular face. Each triangular face has a base of 10 cm and a height of 13 cm. The area of one triangular face is (13/2) * 10 = 65 square centimeters.\nThere are four triangular faces, so the total area of the triangular faces is 4 * 65 = 260 square centimeters.\n\nFinally, the total surface area of the pyramid is the sum of the area of the base and the areas of the four triangular faces.\nThe total surface area is 100 + 260 = 360 square centimeters.",
