      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The total surface area of a pyramid is given by the area of the base plus the area of the four triangular faces.\nSince the base is a square with side length 10 cm, its area is $10^2 = 100$ square centimeters.\nThe four triangular faces can be found by calculating their areas individually and then adding them together.\nThe height of each triangular face is the slant height of the pyramid, which can be found using the Pythagorean theorem.\nThe slant height forms a triangle with the height of the pyramid (12 cm) and half the length of the base (5 cm).\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem, we have $h^2 + 5^2 = 12^2$, which simplifies to $h^2 = 119$ and $h = \\sqrt{119}$.\nThe area of each triangular face is $\\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times \\sqrt{119}$ square centimeters.\nTherefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is $100 + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times \\sqrt{119}$ square centimeters, which simplifies to $\\boxed{100 + 40\\sqrt{119}}$ square centimeters.",
